  "_comment": "Wide and sandy: a slalom through rocks (or the narrow canyon path inside it), a banked hairpin, dune rollers, then the Great Dune: a long climb to the crest of the highest dune in the desert and a glide off its lip, fifteen metres down to the sand flats, then an off-camber bend and boulders rolling across the sandy run home. From lap 2 the quarry tunnel opens under the dune rollers, sandstorms drift over the back road, and on the last lap a dune slumps across the inside of the final bend.",
